(B/'REPORT.txt').write_text('The three authentic native culture contexts have identifiable source inputs: a locked ARCHS4 subset for V1-34 and USZ22, a unique USZ22 column in the declared GSE221532 count file, and a locked USZ23 RefSeq quantification file. Input headers and old accepted source identities were checked without opening GPNMB values or matrix bodies. The deposited USZ22 file is only header/prefix-verified; duplicate NMFH labels and the missing REA title remain unresolved.\n\nThree ordinary annotation-only API calls confirmed human Gene10457/GPNMB and seven current human RefSeq mRNA accessions through official Gene-to-RefSeqRNA links. They establish current annotation, not capture by USZ23 historical transcript quantification. Target-row identity, historical accession completeness and normalization still require an exact separately authorized stage. Missing mapping cannot be called absent RNA.\n\nAll three cultures remain mandatory, with authentic USZ20 and NCC contexts retained where suitable public whole-gene RNA has not been located. Culture libraries are not independent tissue replication; the USZ22 count and ARCHS4 views do not create two biological replicates. Culture selection and incompatible capture/units are alternatives to test. No target difference, protein localization, dependency or drug benefit was measured or inferred. All broader native conditions and suitable pending evidence remain required before promotion.\n')
